From 05045a8dc57a6bc76aaae666ed1e398aaa00cdc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:12:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 130/138] Adaptive Mamba checkpoint retention
 (VLLM_E2_MAMBA_RETAIN_ADAPTIVE_S)

Held prefix checkpoints cost each running request about one block per GDN
group and only pay off while the GPU prefix cache is not churning. With
VLLM_E2_MAMBA_RETAIN_ADAPTIVE_S=N (> 0) the scheduler switches retention off
at the first capacity failure (a waiting request that cannot get blocks, or a
running one before it would be preempted), freeing every held checkpoint into
the cached free queue, and switches it back on after N seconds without one.
Unset/0 keeps static retention.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
